    "https://www.merrimack.edu/obrien-center/": {
      "title": "O’BRIEN CENTER FOR CAREERDEVELOPMENT",
      "description": "Career Resources | Career Development | O’Brien Center Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Combined Majors Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions RESEARCH Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work CATALOGS & CALENDARS Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid STUDENT ACCOUNTS Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus HOUSING & RESIDENCE LIFE DINING Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education STUDENT INVOLVEMENT Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports ON-CAMPUS SERVICES Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search O’BRIEN CENTER FOR CAREER DEVELOPMENT Empowering students to explore future careers and create a personalized path to success Start Your Career Journey with PathwayU Quick Links Home Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Career Services Technology Resources Student Employment Supervisors Recruit Top Talent Corporate Partnerships Events Contact Us Hamburger Toggle Menu Home Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Career Services Technology Resources Student Employment Supervisors Recruit Top Talent Corporate Partnerships Events Contact Us Hamburger Toggle Menu Kickstart Your Career at the O'Brien Center At Merrimack, we’re all about helping you turn your dreams into real career goals. Our O’Brien Center for Career Development gives you the tools, support and guidance to create a personalized career plan and build the skills you need to get there. From guaranteed internships and co-ops to research projects and hands-on experiences, you won’t just learn in the classroom, you’ll learn by doing. And, the answer is yes—it pays off! But at Merrimack College, we empower you to enter the workforce by: Launching your career exploration and development journey the moment you come to Merrimack Using cutting edge technology tools to identify and prepare you for the jobs of the future and create a customized career exploration and development plan Focusing on developing skills that employers are seeking Connecting you to experiential learning and employment opportunities Explore career resources Learn about the Warriors at Work Co-Op Program SUCCESS-DRIVEN EXPLORE. PREPARE. EXPERIENCE. At Merrimack, we believe career preparation is not a one-time event. That’s why Merrimack’s O’Brien Center for Career Development offers four years of programs, resources, connections, and tools, all aimed at one thing: getting you career ready. Job and Internship Listing Networking Events Meet and connect with alumni and professions in your career industry. See Networking Calendar Handshake Search and apply for jobs, internships and co-ops through Handshake. Go to Handshake LinkedIn Learning Access 17,000+ videos to help you develop and enhance your job skills. Visit LinkedIn Learning Career Outcome Rates Merrimack graduates do well in their careeers and with advanced studies. Success After Graduation CAREER MINDED FIND YOUR CAREER PATH. » Link college to career with milestones toward your chosen profession with a Career Action Plan » Meet with your career advisor to explore your strengths, values, and preferences » Get connected to internships, co-ops, or research projects » Draft your resume and cover letters » Participate in a Professional Development Retreat » Begin full-time job interviews and practice salary negotiations » Leverage our alumni/parent/ employer network to launch your job search GO TO HANDSHAKE Lightcast: Labor Market Analytics With Lighcast technology you are able to explore what jobs are in a specific field, how much they are paying, and see the skills you need to pursue that career. As a Merrimack College student, you will dive into your personal Labor Market Analytics Report and create a plan to pursue and talk about skills that make you a desirable candidate for the job or career that you want to pursue. OUR LOCATION McQuade Library Location We are located in the McQuade Library. Contact Information McQuade Library 978-837-5480 [email protected] Facebook-f Twitter Linkedin-in 96% career outcomes rate of 2024 graduates after nine months. 90% of students complete at least one internship or co-op. 100,000+ jobs, co-ops and internships posted in Handshake by 6,800 employers. Request More Info Visit Our Campus Apply Now! Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info Maintenance Requests MyMack Web Editor Login Find People & Places Contact Us Employee Directory Faculty Directory Map and Directions Quick Links Athletics Bookstore Consumer Information Employment Events Calendar Give Library Offices and Services Parking and Transportation Terms of Use Title IX Together We Rise Copyright © 2026 Merrimack College. All Rights Reserved. Search Academics Academics PROGRAM SEARCH Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Combined Majors Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions RESEARCH Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work CATALOGS & CALENDA