    "https://www.merrimack.edu/academics/advising/": {
      "title": "The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising",
      "description": "The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising | Merrimack College Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Combined Majors Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions RESEARCH Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work CATALOGS & CALENDARS Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid STUDENT ACCOUNTS Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus HOUSING & RESIDENCE LIFE DINING Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education STUDENT INVOLVEMENT Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports ON-CAMPUS SERVICES Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Academics The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising Schools and Programs Quick Links Home Academic Advising Career Advising Financial Aid Advising MackForce Central Help Desk Who is my Advisor? Faculty & Staff Home Academic Advising Career Advising Financial Aid Advising MackForce Central Help Desk Who is my Advisor? Faculty & Staff Academic & Career Advising Concierge-Level Advising for Your Undergraduate Journey The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising provides seamless and personalized undergraduate support from your first day at Merrimack through Commencement. As an undergraduate student, you will be paired with a dedicated advisor who will follow you throughout your Merrimack experience and tailor your support based on your academic, career, financial and personal needs. Hours Mon-Thurs: 8 a.m.-5 p.m. Friday: 8 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Location The Lucey Center McQuade Library Advising Made Simple We make it easy for you to connect with your academic, career, and financial aid advisors whenever you need support. From choosing classes to planning your career and managing college costs, our advisors are here to guide you every step of the way. We offer the following services in The Lucey Center: Academic Advising Services Offering personalized guidance on your academic success and support. Academic Advising Career Advising Services Working with you to discover your passions and career path. Career Advising Financial Aid Advising Services Offering individualized advising on your financial aid and support. Financial Aid Advising Academic Advising Services The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising - McQuade Library, First Floor Our academic advisors in The Lucey Center offer concierge-level support to help you thrive. Our centralized advising model offers a dynamic space to explore your academic and professional goals, preparing you for success beyond college. We offer personalized guidance in areas such as: Academic Requirements Academics & Social Life Management Major, Minor or Concentration Options Degree Pathways & Progress Course Registration Outside-the-Classroom Activities Meet the Academic Advising Team WALK-UP CONCIERGE STUDENT SUPPORT The Mack Force Central Help Desk Located on the first floor of the McQuade Library, The MackForce Central is your go-to destination for answers. Whether you need to schedule an appointment, complete a transaction, or get pointed in the right direction, we’re here to help. Stop by for solutions related to: Class Registration Parking & Transportation Meal Plans Graduation Requirements Campus Events And more! Learn More About The Mack Force Career Advising Services The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising - McQuade Library, First Floor Lucey Center career advisors help you discover what you can do with your major. We are here, alongside your academic advisor, to help you choose the right major that best aligns with your goals. We will help you build the confidence and skills you need to succeed in interviews and assist you in narrowing down your job search. We also offer guidance on graduate school and ways to develop your leadership and communication skills. We offer personalized guidance in areas such as: Networking & Mentorships Resumes, Cover Letters & Portfolios Internships & Experiential Learning Interview Preparation Job Search Strategies Salary Negotiation Meet the Career Advising Team Cohort & Graduate Student Support Compass, Honors & Warriors at Work Students If you are a member of the Honors program, Compass, or Warriors at Work, you will receive specialized support and continue to be assigned advisors within your program. Meet the Compass Advising Team Meet the Honors Advising Team Meet the Warriors at Work Advising Team Graduate & Doctoral Students Our graduate and doctoral students will continue to be advised through their academic program, and will also have access to all of the student support services located in McQuade Library. Financial Aid Advising Services Financial Aid Office - Austin Hall, First Floor Our financial aid advisors provide guidance on available options and resources, helping you plan for expenses and develop a strategic financial plan as you work toward your degree. We offer personalized guidance in areas such as: Financial Aid Options Budgeting Guidance Long-Term Financial Planning Award Letter Review Loan Counseling Scholarship Searches Meet the Financial Aid Advising Team Who is my advisor? Don't know who your advisor is? Log into myMack and select student advising. Your advisors will be listed. Log Into myMack Visual & Performing Arts Student Spotlight: Mia Sukeforth ’25 Mia Sukeforth tells us about her fabulous internship! Request More Info Visit Our Campus Apply Now! Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info 