    "https://www.merrimack.edu/academics/graduate/fellowships/": {
      "title": "Graduate Fellowships",
      "description": "Graduate Fellowships Merrimack College | Graduate Programs Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Combined Majors Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions RESEARCH Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work CATALOGS & CALENDARS Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid STUDENT ACCOUNTS Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus HOUSING & RESIDENCE LIFE DINING Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education STUDENT INVOLVEMENT Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports ON-CAMPUS SERVICES Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Graduate Programs Graduate Fellowships Schools and Programs › Graduate Programs Apply Now Find Your Graduate Program Graduate Fellowships Reduce your graduate education costs and gain unparalleled professional experience with a fellowship at Merrimack College. Graduate Admission Graduate Tuition & Fees Scholarships & Financial Aid Graduate Career Resources CONTACT US Questions? Please contact us at [email protected] or at 978-837-3563 . Benefits of Graduate Fellowships Merrimack is committed to making your master’s degree affordable while providing you with immersive, hands-on paraprofessional experiences. Our graduate fellowships offer: Affordability with Steep Tuition Discounts. Offered in most of our master’s degree programs, these competitive fellowship opportunities put your career on the fast-track while providing a tuition discount of 50-100%. High-impact Professional Experience. You’ll build your professional experience while saving thousands on tuition. Fellowships offer unparalleled opportunities for developing high-level, real-world skills in your field of expertise. Access to Faculty and Staff Mentors. With the guidance of experienced site-based supervisors and Merrimack faculty mentors, you’ll have the support you need to excel in your field placement and in your graduate studies. Types of Graduate Fellowships Merrimack offers three graduate fellowships. Explore fellowship opportunities by school to determine details and types of fellowships available. Looking for scholarship info? Presidential Fellowship The Presidential Fellowship provides 100% of a student’s graduate tuition and includes a 9-month, 25 hour per week, unpaid fellowship placement. Please note: College-funded fellowships may be awarded, competitively, to students who have been admitted to a graduate program and who are academically eligible. In order to maintain eligibility for a graduate fellowship, a student must be enrolled full-time and must maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 3.0. We offer many placements that provide training and experience in the program area in which the student is enrolled and is intended for the educational benefit of the student. Receipt of the fellowship and placement does not create an employment relationship with Merrimack and does not include any wages or monetary remuneration besides the tuition benefit. This fellowship includes either an on-campus or off-campus placement. Students limited to 20 hours a week for the unpaid fellowship (e.g., international students, etc.) will work with the program director/dean to arrange and account for an additional 5-hour-a-week research component that may include (up to 5 hours per week) scheduled meeting time with the respective program director/dean/designated instructor. If you are offered and accept a fellowship position, you will not be eligible for any other discounts or scholarships, including a merit-based Dean scholarship or the Double Warrior alumni scholarship . If you are originally awarded a scholarship and then are given a fellowship placement, you will no longer receive the merit scholarship. The fellowship award will replace any other discounts. and scholarships. For two year programs: Fellowships are only awarded and applied for the first year of the program (up to 36 credits) EXCEPT for our M.S. in Biology, M.S. in Mechanical Engineering, and M.S. in Civil Engineering – these three programs have fellowship positions that offer two years of tuition coverage and require between 15 and 25 hours per week . Graduate fellows will not be eligible for a scholarship in the second year of the program. Provost Fellowship The Provost Fellowship provides 50% of a student’s graduate tuition and includes a 9-month, 15 hour per week, unpaid fellowship placement. Please note: College-funded fellowships may be awarded, competitively, to those students who have been admitted to a graduate program and who are academically eligible. In order to maintain eligibility for a graduate fellowship, a student must be currently enrolled full-time in classes in a specific degree program and must maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 3.0. We offer many placements that provide training and experience in the program area in which the student is enrolled and is intended for the educational benefit of the student. This fellowship includes either an on-campus or off-campus fellowship placement. Receipt of the fellowship and placement does not create an employment relationship with Merrimack and does not include any wages or monetary remuneration besides the tuition benefit. If you are offered and accept a fellowship position, you will not be eligible for any other discounts or scholarships, including a merit-based Dean scholarship or the Double Warrior alumni scholarship . If you are originally awarded a scholarship and then are given a fellowship placement, you will no longer receive the merit scholarship. The fellowship award will replace any other discounts and scholarships. For two year programs , fellowships are only awarded during their first fellowship year (up to 36 credits). Graduate fellows are not eligible for additional scholarship in the second year of the program K-12 Teacher Education Fellowship This K-12 Teacher Education Fellowship provides a non-credit fellowship course and a full-time, 10-month placement. This off-campus fellowship and placement provides intensive clinical experience and will provide training and experience in the education area in which the student is enrolled and is intended for the educational benefit of the student. Please note: This Fellowship provides 100% of the student’s graduate tuition; the tuition is covered by the school or district where the placement occurs. Receipt of the fellowship and placement does not create an employment relationship with Merrimack and does not include any wages or monetary remuneration besides the tuition benefit. If you are offered and accept a fellowship position, you will not be eligible for any other discounts or scholarships, including a merit-based Dean scholarship or the Double Warrior alumni scholarship . If you are originally awarded a scholarship and then are given a fellowship placement, you will no longer receive the merit scholarship. The fellowship award will replace any other discounts. Fellowship Opportunities by School Graduate School of Counseling and Social Work Designed to prepare distinguished and accomplished professionals, our programs equip graduates with the skills and mindset to not only create change, but to positively impact the communities they serve. See Counseling and Social Work Fellowships School of Education and Social Policy Our education and social policy fellowships allow you to work at the College or a partner institution where you’ll get first-rate professional experience and build skills that set you apart in the job market. See Education and Social Policy Fellowships School of Nursing & Health Sciences Merrimack College’s one-of-a-kind health sciences fellowships offer a hands-on experience that you can’t get in a classroom. You’ll work in a professional practice while enjoying a reduction in your tuition. See School of Nursing & Health Sciences Fellowships School of Arts & Sciences You can earn while you learn via one of Merrimack’s fellowships in the School of Arts & Sciences. These competitive awards provide supervised work experience with a tuition discount. See Arts & Sciences Fellowships School of Engineering & Computational Sciences Merrimack’s Engineering & Computational Sciences fellowships seek to enrich professional qualifications and help advance career goals through valuable hands-on experience while covering the cost of tuition for highly qualified graduate students. See Engineering & Computational Sciences Fellowships Please note that we do not currently offer fellowships or merit-based scholarships for any Girard School of Business graduate programs. However, students in the Girard School of Business are eligible for our Double Warrior Alumni Scholarship and associated benefits. It’s Easy to Apply for a Fellowship Online HOW TO APPLY Click the “Apply Now” button below or go to gps.merrimack.edu/apply to begin or resume your graduate application. Within your app, select “Yes” for “Are you applying to a fellowship?” Submit your application. Be sure to complete the required Fellowship essay. Receive your admission decision. If admitted to the master’s program, you’ll receive further instructions about the fellowship process. Apply Now The Chronicle of Higher Education Fastest-Growing Private Nonprofit Institution - Master’s Merrimack College was recognized by The Chronicle of Higher Education as the 10th fastest-growing private nonprofit institution in the Master’s category. In the last 10 years, Merrimack’s graduate enrollment has increased 148%. Send Me Info Merrimack’s graduate fellowships make earning your master’s degree more affordable while providing you hands-on professional experience. Fellows receive tuition support, gain real-world skills through placements, and work closely with faculty and staff mentors. Please complete this  form so a member of our graduate admissions team can follow up with details and guidance on applying. \" * \" indicates required fields Δ Name This field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged. Your Name * First Name Last Name Email Address * Mobile Number * Program of Interest * Please Select Master in Nonprofit Management and Community Engagement (M.Ed.) Master of Arts in Communication Master of Education in School Counseling Master of Education in Teacher Education Master of Public Administration (Online) Master of Science in Applied Chemistry Master of Science in Biology Master of Science in Civil Engineering Master of Science in Clinical Mental Health Counseling Master of Science in Criminology and Criminal Justice (Online) Master of Science in Exercise and Sport Science Master of Science in Health Promotion and Management Master of Science in Mechanical Engineering Master of Science in Speech-Language Pathology Master of Social Work Include SLP prerequisite information Include SLP prerequisite information This field is hidden when viewing the form Available Terms - Summer Only Select Term Summer 2027 Summer 2028 Summer 2029 Summer 2030 Available Terms - Fall Only * Select Term Fall 2027 Fall 2028 Fall 2029 Fall 2030 This field is hidden when viewing the form Available Terms - Spring / Summer Only Select Term Spring 2027 Spring 2028 Spring 2029 Spring 2030 Summer 2027 Summer 2028 Summer 2029 Summer 2030 This field is hidden when viewing the form Available Terms - Fall / Summer Only Select Term Fall 2027 Fall 2028 Fall 2029 Fall 2030 Summer 2027 Summer 2028 Summer 2029 Summer 2030 Available Terms - Fall / Spring Only * Select Term Fall 2027 Fall 2028 Fall 2029 Fall 2030 Spring 2027 Spring 2028 Spring 2029 Spring 2030 Available Terms - Fall / Spring / Summer * Select Term F