    "https://www.merrimack.edu/news/tolle-lege-reception-celebrates-faculty-research-scholarship/": {
      "title": "NEWS & EVENTS",
      "description": "Tolle Lege Reception Celebrates Faculty Research, Scholarship | Merrimack College Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Combined Majors Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions RESEARCH Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work CATALOGS & CALENDARS Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid STUDENT ACCOUNTS Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus HOUSING & RESIDENCE LIFE DINING Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education STUDENT INVOLVEMENT Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports ON-CAMPUS SERVICES Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search OFFICE OF COMMUNICATIONS AND MARKETING NEWS & EVENTS Campus News › Tolle Lege Reception Celebrates Faculty Research, Scholarship Quick Links Home Our Work Podcasts Publications Videos Branding Toolkit and Policies Web Resources and Policies Meet the Staff For Journalists News Notable & Quotable Report Website Accessibility Issues Hamburger Toggle Menu Home Our Work Podcasts Publications Videos Branding Toolkit and Policies Web Resources and Policies Meet the Staff For Journalists News Notable & Quotable Report Website Accessibility Issues Hamburger Toggle Menu Tolle Lege Reception Celebrates Faculty Research, Scholarship Now in its 22nd year, the Tolle Lege Reception honors the published works of Merrimack College faculty, staff, students and alumni. In 2024, more than 150 pieces were published by members of the Merrimack community. May 2, 2025 | By: Michael Cronin As Merrimack College continues its transformation into a leading Catholic research university, some of the faculty contributing to that transformation were recently celebrated. Three Merrimack faculty members helping to foster a culture of research were honored at the College’s annual Tolle Lege Reception on Wednesday, April 30, in the Collegiate Church of Christ the Teacher. The honorees represent critical aspects of the College’s research ecosystem, from student support to new faculty research. Anthony Fernandez, professor of chemistry and biochemistry, received the Outstanding Research Mentorship Award for his efforts to help his students achieve their research goals. “He has mentored over 20 graduate and undergraduate students during his time at Merrimack,” said April Bowling, vice president for research and vice provost for graduate innovation, who presented the awards. “Anthony is the quintessential heart of the type of faculty that makes Merrimack the place it is today. He has tirelessly and selflessly contributed to the development of our students and junior faculty.” Juliana Cohen, professor of nutrition and public health, was recognized with the Spirit of Discovery Award for the opportunities her research has provided her students. “She and her four undergraduate and graduate research assistants are currently in California collecting data for her next big study,” Bowling explained. “Her research centers on the identification, evaluation and dissemination of effective school policies and initiatives to address diet-related disparities and reduce the risk of obesity amongst children.” The Early Career Researcher Award, which recognizes a faculty member in their first three years at Merrimack who has shown immense productivity in their field, was given to Amy Shafrir, assistant professor in health sciences and nutrition. In 2024, Shafrir published 10 research papers on pelvic pain and endometriosis. “It’s not lost on me that I was on the hiring committee for (Shafrir),” Bowling said. “She personifies that you can be an incredibly productive researcher, an incredibly impactful teacher and a contributor to the curriculum and progress of your school.” Now in its 22nd year, the Tolle Lege Reception celebrates the recent inductees into the McQuade Library’s Tolle Lege Collection, which catalogs published work from Merrimack faculty, students and alumni. The collection added 155 pieces published in 2024 by more than 100 Merrimack authors. “(Starting in 2003,) now-retired library director Barbara LaChance and former Merrimack College Augustinian the Rev. Jim Wenzel, O.S.A., wanted to acknowledge and celebrate Merrimack’s growing community of authors,” explained Lyena Chavez, head librarian at McQuade Library. “Now a tradition every year, McQuade librarians curate a special collection of Merrimack community publications and host an event honoring Merrimack’s authors of the past year.” SHARE THIS ARTICLE Related News Sparked at Merrimack: Alumnus Launches AI Motion-Capture Startup August 31, 2026 | By: Ashley LoPresti 3 MIN READ A biomechanics fellowship sparked one exercise science student's passion for motion analysis; a passion he channeled into founding his own company and building an application that addresses a need for better technology. READ MORE Graduate Senate President has Lifelong Experience in Community Service February 19, 2026 | By: Michael Cronin 3 MIN READ Sonya Dhanpat M’27 is currently enrolled in Merrimack College’s community engagement graduate program. READ MORE Merrimack Welcomes Former Bishop of Chulucanas, Peru April 8, 2026 | By: Michael Cronin 3 MIN READ Bishop Daniel Turley, O.S.A., served in Peru for over 50 years. READ MORE Office of Communications and Marketing The Summer Research Institute at Merrimack College Merrimack’s research-focused faculty and staff develop programming to build students research skills in academia. Request More Info Visit Our Campus Apply Now! Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover,